Based on the retrieved context, specifically Source 1, to configure an incremental model in dbt, you can use the `on_schema_change` parameter.

You can set it to `append_new_columns` to append new columns to the existing table. This setting does not remove columns from the existing table that are not present in the new data.

Here is an example:
```
{{
  config(
    materialized='incremental',
    on_schema_change='append_new_columns'
  )
}}
```
This will allow dbt to continue running incremental models in the presence of schema changes, resulting in fewer `--full-refresh` scenarios and saving query costs.

Note that this setting does not backfill values in old records for newly added columns. If you need to populate those values, you will need to run manual updates or trigger a `--full-refresh`.
